{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-177457",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $4$ is even or ${4}^{2}=12.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{ is even }}_{⏟}}_{M}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{{4}^{2}=12}_{⏟}}_{N},\n$$\n\nthat is, $M∨N.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $-2$ is an integer number. This corresponds to $P.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{ is even}\\text{ or }{4}^{2}=12}_{⏟}}_{M\\,∨\\,N},\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{-2\\text{ is an integer number}}_{⏟}}_{P}\n$$\n\nthat is, $(M∨N)∧P.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-177457\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"515\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2227\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∧</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"516\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2228\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∨</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>\".</p>\n<p>Note that this sentence consists of two parts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Part 1:</strong> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"517\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is even or <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"518\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn 